Subject: Hoist only requires the load to be the register's last write

What this does
  Hoist only requires the load to be the register's last write.

Why we need it
  The strict "written nowhere else in the IR" form refused every loop whose bound shares a register with a preheader value, because the reload inside the loop makes the bound's live range end at the test.

What it adds
  `defs` now records the last write per physical register and the check is `defs[pr] == ti`: an earlier write is overwritten by the load before the loop, and any write after the load is unsafe, so the last-write form is both weaker and sufficient.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index 95ecbb2..9d899c8 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
